call.content:
{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "action": "answer",
  "response": null,
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "c1",
      "text": "In the DPO findings for a 1.5B model, both train loss and reward accuracy indicated 'great run' status while behavioral evaluation found otherwise.",
      "citation_ids": ["S1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "c2",
      "text": "The lesson drawn from this discrepancy is that pressure-resistance decouples from correctness when optimization amplifies confidence without adding knowledge.",
      "citation_ids": ["S1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "c3",
      "text": "In sweep findings for a 1.5B model, the best train loss (worst generalizer) validated that optimizing imitation does not align with behavioral objectives like calibration.",
      "citation_ids": ["S3"]
    },
    {
      "id": "c4",
      "text": "The deployed r16 model remains selected because it maintains better calibration compared to the best eval loss configuration (r64), despite lower general scores in behavioral evaluations.",
      "citation_ids": ["S3"]
    }
  ]
}

